        "BODY": "Grayscale has been pushing forward with its plan to convert the closed-end Dogecoin Trust into an exchange-traded fund. The revised S-1 filing, submitted to the SEC, details Coinbase as the chosen broker and custodian. If approved, the DOGE ETF will trade under the ticker GDOG on NYSE Arca. This filing follows the SEC’s recent approval of new standards for crypto funds, which could streamline the launch of multiple exchange-traded products in the coming months. Against this backdrop, attention is turning to whether Mutuum Finance (MUTM) can outperform Dogecoin and position itself as the next crypto to hit $1. Dogecoin ETF Progress The submission of Grayscale’s updated S-1 comes amid heightened ETF activity in the crypto market. NYSE Arca has also proposed updates for Grayscale’s Ethereum Trust and its mini version to align with simplified SEC rules. These changes build on the SEC’s approval of listing standards, including the requirement that digital assets should have a futures market regulated in the United States for at least six months. Because Dogecoin already has futures and options trading on regulated exchanges, Grayscale is arguing that DOGE qualifies for this structure. Despite this progress, the firm is not yet offering in-kind creation and redemption, which could limit flexibility for institutional investors. Nevertheless, the push for a Dogecoin ETF signals broader acceptance of meme tokens in structured financial products. Yet while DOGE gains a regulated pathway, investors are considering whether its growth potential matches that of newer altcoins like Mutuum Finance. Mutuum Finance Presale Growth Mutuum Finance (MUTM) is currently in Phase 6 of its presale, priced at $0.035, a 250% increase from the opening phase price of $0.01. So far, $16,200,000 has been raised, and 16,500 holders have joined. The presale is selling out fast, and once Phase 6 ends, Phase 7 will open at $0.04, marking a 14.3% rise. At launch, MUTM will list at $0.06, meaning current buyers can secure returns of 371% after listing. The project is not just relying on hype. It is building a decentralized lending and borrowing platform where users can earn yield on deposits or unlock liquidity against existing holdings. Overcollateralization, liquidation safeguards, and borrow caps ensure that the system remains stable during volatile market swings. Borrowers can choose variable or stable rates, and deposit caps further protect against outsized exposure. This risk-focused framework is helping Mutuum earn credibility in the crypto investment space. Security And Incentives Mutuum Finance has passed its CertiK audit at 90/100, indicating a high security posture of the token scan. Additionally, the team rewards managed to kickstart a Bug Bounty Program with a total reward pool of $50,000 USDT to be distributed across four levels. This ensures that, in the long term, even the smallest loopholes are fixed by building trust in the protocol. The project has also announced a giveaway for MUTM, which is worth $100,000 , which is split among 10 winners to receive $10,000 each. To be qualified, participants need to invest minimum at least $50 in the presale and perform simple tasks, and provide a wallet address. Mutuum also has a leaderboard dashboard whereby the top 50 holders will receive bonus tokens for holding their position. These efforts are building momentum for engagement within the community and providing some hard-set rewards for early adopters. Why Mutuum Is Gaining Traction Mutuum Finance is already separating itself from older tokens by focusing on practical use cases. Its borrowing and lending structure relies on Chainlink oracles for price accuracy, while fallback oracles and aggregated feeds ensure continuity. This reliability is vital for protecting liquidity during market swings. Consequently, MUTM is gaining traction as not just another new crypto coin, but a project anchored in tested DeFi mechanisms. Moreover, while Dogecoin waits on ETF approval, MUTM is giving direct exposure to a utility-driven model in active presale stages. The platform’s roadmap includes an over-collateralized stablecoin, further expanding its role in DeFi lending. These developments are encouraging crypto investing discussions around MUTM as one of the best cryptos to buy now, especially given the structured tokenomics and growing presale numbers. Looking Ahead To The Next Crypto To Hit $1 Mutuum Finance has been proving that new crypto coins with real utility can capture market interest quickly. Dogecoin’s ETF path may bring it more legitimacy, but MUTM’s presale momentum, security milestones, and lending use case are driving strong demand today. The fact that Phase 6 is nearing completion underscores how rapidly investors are moving in. Therefore, while Grayscale’s DOGE ETF submission signals another step for meme coins, Mutuum Finance is positioning itself as the altcoin that could realistically emerge as the next crypto to hit $1. Those entering now are locking in a price point that could deliver substantial returns when the token officially launches. For more information about Mutuum Finance (MUTM) visit the links below: Website: https://mutuum.com/ Linktree: https://linktr.ee/mutuumfinance Disclaimer: This is a sponsored press release for informational purposes only. It does not reflect the views of Times Tabloid, nor is it intended to be used as legal, tax, investment, or financial advice. Times Tabloid is not responsible for any financial losses. The post Can Mutuum Finance Beat DOGE As The Next Crypto To Hit $1 Amid Grayscale Submission of Revised S-1 for Dogecoin ETF appeared first on Times Tabloid .",
